WEBVTT

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.040
It was the day before Kou Shuurei departed for Sashuu.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.350
It's unusual for you to call me, Seiran.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.540
Is this an invitation for a date?

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:46.080
No way.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:47.010
Take this.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:49.960
Kanshou?

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:56.430
The great sword Kanshou was forged from the same ore that produced Bakuya, the Emperor's sword.

00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:01.010
The two are twin swords that Ryuuki had entrusted to Seiran.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.970
Please give this to Ensei in Sashuu.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:06.120
To Ensei-dono?

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:07.060
Yes.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:12.620
I see. He's fortunate that you care so much about him.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.620
I don't care about him. It's just that...

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.610
Never mind. You'll understand when you give this to him.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:24.580
I understand. I'll take care of it.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.260
I will not fail to give this to Ensei-dono.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:32.370
Well, knowing that guy, he'll probably just say "Hell" and not be grateful for it.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.630
I suppose so.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:39.340
I will deliver Kanshou and Shuurei-dono safely.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:40.840
I trust this to you.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:55.050
Ran Shuuei delivered Kanshou safely into Ensei's hands.

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:00.640
Huh? This is the sword he got from the Emperor!

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.260
Yes. It's Kanshou.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:04.930
What was he thinking?

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.190
I can't use swords.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.620
He should know that too...

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:19.310
Meanwhile, Shuurei met up with Ensei and told him her resolution.

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:23.780
Please, Ensei.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.920
If my head is what's needed...

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:30.560
then behead me without hesitation.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:45.410
That illness existed long before you were born.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:49.290
Your death won't cure a single person. You do know that, right?

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:49.930
Yes.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.120
Well then, what you're telling me to do is exactly what Jyasen-kyou wants.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:57.670
Exactly what those idiots that ramble on about you causing the disease want.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:02.850
If chaos ensues and treatment is delayed because of me, all our efforts will've been wasted.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.340
We must prioritize treatment over everything else!

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.580
Well, yeah...

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.110
I'll explain and try to persuade people until the very last moment...

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:15.150
but perhaps they won't listen because they believe I caused the disease.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:20.110
The moment might arise when only a remedy called Kou Shuurei will suffice...

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:27.070
Seiran couldn't do it, but maybe Ensei can.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.690
Your highest priority isn't to protect me, is it?

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:34.840
You're an officer of Sashuu.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:38.210
You're telling me to kill you, Princess?

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:45.610
You're telling me to live on after killing you, with the burden of hatred

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:49.720
from Shouka, Seiran, and all the others who like you?

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:54.440
Please. I cannot ask anyone but you right now.

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:59.600
Seiran couldn't do it, so I should?

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:06.740
Princess, what is your best case scenario?

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:08.770
My best case scenario?

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:09.610
Yeah.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.470
There are people who trust me and are waiting for me.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:17.620
I can't give my life away carelessly.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:27.910
I'll protect everything I can, including myself.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:32.260
For that, I'll do anything. I'll come home alive.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:34.340
Very well.

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:39.580
I can't trust a boss who's thinking about dying from the outset.

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:43.240
You never know when the boss will kill himself to get away from the responsibility.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:50.230
Anyway, if that moment comes, that means there's no other way, right?

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:55.360
If that moment comes, I won't let anyone get in my way.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:59.040
I'll take responsibility for your life.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:00.850
Ensei!

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:09.520
Even if Seiran were to hate me and chase after me forever, I'll deliver your head to Shouka and the Emperor.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.890
What?! Did you just say something gross?

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.790
You said it first, Princess.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:20.490
"In the worst case, please take care of it.
I cannot ask anyone but you," right?

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:22.590
R-Right, but...

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.530
Come to think of it, this is incredible!

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:29.030
Aren't you showing me more love than Seiran?

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:35.330
Well, Seiran would probably just find an excuse and run away.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.200
Yeah, he would. Definitely.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:41.830
But...

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.510
He entrusted this to me.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.300
That means he's beginning to understand.

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:53.180
Huh?

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:54.100
Nothing...

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:02.730
By the way, have you heard about Eigetsu?

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:06.920
I decided to take all possible steps beforehand to treat the disease...

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.040
Time to go and meet Eigetsu-kun, Ensei!

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:14.160
Yeah!

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:30.000
Yougetsu...

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:36.970
What Jyasen-kyou wanted was you, Yougetsu...

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:51.400
Yougetsu... for you, and not for me,

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:53.990
I can't die yet!

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:56.710
Kourin-san...

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:00.610
I always gave you a hard time.

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:03.330
Please... live a happy life...

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:20.910
You still greet me with a scary face, Eigetsu.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:29.630
My adorable child.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:47.280
Is that them?

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:47.750
Yes, sir!

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:56.060
Riou, look!

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:57.470
Hurry up!

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:03.090
Hold, hold.

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:12.250
There are doctors coming to our village to treat the disease.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:15.360
Do you know where they are right now?

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:33.050
It can't be. You've come all the way from Sekiei Village?

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:36.550
We have. We wanted to save everyone.

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:40.760
Surprisingly, everyone has stayed alive.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:45.060
N-No way... Did you bring all the patients from the village?!

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:45.650
We did.

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:49.790
You fools! What if the disease spreads to this region?!

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:54.660
Shuon! How many times do I have to tell you that the disease can't spread from person to person?!

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:57.450
Ah, yes, but what if...

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:19.430
Very well. Every single one of you will be accommodated in Korin Castle.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:26.730
M-Mayor! We can't possibly accept the sick into our city!

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:29.170
The citizens around the castle won't agree to it!

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:29.850
Shut up!

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:34.080
In my hometown, the people with strange diseases were just kicked out!

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:37.610
It's best if we burn the village, including the sick...

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:48.170
He'll be dismissed and exiled from Koringun.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:50.800
Mayor Hei should not dirty his hands for this man.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:11:01.300
Mayor, I admire your morals, but the people of the city are already under stress because of Governor Kou.

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:06.860
If you accept the sick as well, the situation may become dangerous.

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:12.340
Many of the citizens, like Shuon, won't listen, no matter how many times you explain.

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:18.670
What exactly was our job? Our duty?

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.990
What was it we were supposed to protect?

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:28.950
I order you once again. We're accepting them. All of them!

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:35.460
They are people of Koringun too!

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:41.430
My mother was left on the mountain because of an illness.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:44.770
As a child, by the time I was able to go to her, she had already...

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:49.970
You're doing this for personal reasons, but I am grateful for your decision.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.450
I will humbly do as you command.

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:39.860
I never imagined this happening.

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:43.650
Cutting up beasts and camping out...

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.740
My mother would be in tears if she found out.

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:51.140
But we can save those who are suffering from disease with our own hands!

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:52.620
Let's do our best!

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:58.200
You need much, much more practice.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:00.880
Ah, You-sensei.

00:13:01.310 --> 00:13:04.850
Nonetheless, I think everyone has improved a lot.

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:10.640
Everything is cut up neatly. It's much easier to cook them.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:11.550
You think so?

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:16.370
In fact, they need more practice on sutures than incisions.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:20.010
The stitches are so ragged that I can't bear to see them.

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:28.660
Hmm, but after all, the incisions are far more important than the stitches.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:32.910
So long as the contents don't spill out, it doesn't matter if the stitches are a bit irregular.

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:34.660
Is that so?

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:41.350
That's right! If you can make people at the feast laugh about your stitches, it will be a bonus!

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:46.750
Um, Princess, this old man <i>is</i> some kind of amazing doctor, right?

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:47.930
He's not a fake, is he?

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:51.800
How dare you! What do you mean by "a fake"?!

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:54.330
I have a plan for the sutures.

00:13:54.830 --> 00:14:00.320
The main problem is that most of them don't know what this will be like in reality.

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:04.570
I put the highest importance on stamina and selected only young people.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:06.820
In addition, most of them are from good families.

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:09.520
Theory and practice are completely different.

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:11.420
If they don't approach this with courage,

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:14.070
not only will they be in our way, they might lose their minds.

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:18.970
Well, I did try to pick out optimistic ones.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:22.260
Governor Kou, Officer Rou.

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:26.200
We have received some new information, but...

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:27.950
Rin-san?

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.130
First of all, this is from Shunki-dono.

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:36.080
Kourin-dono has gone after Eigetsu-dono and left Sekiei Village on her own.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:38.140
On her own?!

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:43.800
While Shunki-dono was away at the government offices to get an elite soldier as Kourin's bodyguard,

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.430
Kourin-dono packed up and left on her own.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:49.130
Why was she in such a hurry?

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:52.280
Eigetsu didn't go there to die.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:54.870
She could've waited for a bodyguard.

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:56.310
Go there to die...

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:02.280
Not far in the future, To Eigetsu will be gone from this world.

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:05.750
Eigetsu-kun...

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.880
As far as I could find out,

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:14.310
Kourin joined the Merchants Guild's carriages that were heading towards Sekiei Village, as a cook.

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:19.390
It's the method you used before! She copied you.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:24.790
Kourin-dono is acting deliberately, so don't worry about her for now.

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:25.850
But...

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:30.780
We might be able to meet Kourin-dono at Korin Castle.

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:32.320
Why is that?

00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:36.280
There's no one in Sekiei Village now.

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:43.920
All the villagers have already arrived at Korin Castle, including the sick.

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:49.030
They came down from the mountain to obtain treatment as soon as possible.

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:53.550
The carriages of the Merchants Guild are also going to Korin Castle,

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:55.890
so we should be able to meet Kourin-dono soon.

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:09.570
Huh? Hold, hold!

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:12.680
Hey, what's wrong?

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:16.680
Please, don't mind me and go ahead!

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.050
What?

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:20.050
Thank you for everything.

00:16:20.940 --> 00:16:24.000
Hey! There's no one left in Sekiei Village anymore!

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:24.890
That's not true!

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:28.750
I heard a rumor on the way here.

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:34.880
A boy about the age of 13 or 14, who was working among the doctors, has gone missing from Sekiei Village.

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:43.120
I must go and look...

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:44.480
for him.

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:50.610
Mayor Hei had overridden the objections of the citizens and taken all the villagers into the castle.

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:53.490
He is waiting for our arrival. That's the message.

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.500
Ensei, how much longer will it take to get to Korin Castle?

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:00.180
If we do a forced march, we can get there by dawn.

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:07.370
We'll pack all the edible parts immediately and take them with us.

00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:10.710
If it's a matter of our own stamina, we cannot leave the meat behind!

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:13.520
Awesome! I'm a bit more cheerful now!

00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:15.570
Well, in that case, I'll get on with the preparations for departure.

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.310
We'll leave at half-past four!

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.080
Tomorrow morning...

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:29.490
Seriously?

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:34.840
What is this?! You're all looking as if you've lost your souls!

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:36.950
Now, get on with it!

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.030
You know what you're supposed to do, right?

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:40.960
Um... You-sensei...

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:43.830
Grrr! Shut up! Stop whining!

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:47.320
We don't have time for that! Stop thinking and get moving!

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:48.290
Yes, sir!

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:51.070
What you will do when you face the patients?

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:54.670
Whether or not you'll be ready at that moment is up to you.

00:17:58.630 --> 00:18:00.870
I must hurry without a moment's delay.

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:03.640
There are people who are waiting for our help!

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:11.010
Kill the woman governor?!

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:13.150
That's right.

00:18:13.390 --> 00:18:16.290
The mayor ordered us to welcome her with respect.

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:19.150
Besides, you were exiled from Koringun, weren't you?

00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:21.750
Are you trying to take revenge on the mayor?

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:23.770
This isn't about some petty revenge.

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:24.550
What?

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:28.190
This woman governor caused an outbreak of disease.

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:31.040
She intends to spread the disease in Korin too.

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:35.230
The mayor told us that the woman governor didn't cause the disease.

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:37.420
Then what did cause it?!

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:42.260
The disease began to spread as soon as that woman became governor!

00:18:43.870 --> 00:18:47.190
But we can't disobey our mayor's orders...

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:47.670
Yeah.

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:50.090
She's a woman who can spread disease.

00:18:50.090 --> 00:18:53.810
If she has the power to do that, it'd be a piece of cake for her to control the mayor.

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:56.630
You mean she's using witchcraft.

00:18:56.980 --> 00:18:59.380
It all makes sense, doesn't it?

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:05.790
The woman governor must be killed!

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:10.050
That is the way to protect the mayor and Koringun!

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:10.910
Isn't that right?!

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:12.300
I understand!

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:14.190
The flag indicating their arrival will be the signal!

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:15.350
We'll attack her all together!

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:16.600
Hear, hear!

00:19:32.390 --> 00:19:34.080
There's really no one here...

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:41.120
No! I won't wait.

00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:44.740
I don't expect anything from him anymore!

00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:47.760
I like you.

00:19:50.050 --> 00:19:53.730
So, please forget about me and live a happy life.

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:06.400
Always saying what <i>he</i> wants.

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:09.270
He didn't even ask me to go with him.

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:13.310
I'll take what I want with my own hands.

00:20:14.210 --> 00:20:15.800
I'm going to look for you!

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:22.400
You must be the woman governor!

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:48.120
We've finally arrived.

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:49.470
Yeah.

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:53.130
We rode all night. Are you feeling all right, Princess?

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:54.100
Yeah.

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:57.810
What's wrong, Ensei?

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:00.490
This will be a bit of a problem.

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:09.230
Mayor Hei!

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:10.950
This is serious!

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:12.700
What is it?

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:20.040
Bring my horse! Now!

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:21.250
Y-Yes.

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:33.160
The gate!

00:21:33.970 --> 00:21:36.640
Rin! Old man You! Wait here!

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:47.880
Princess, hold on tight!

00:21:52.310 --> 00:21:54.280
They're telling us to turn back.

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:57.600
Or else they're gonna aim at us next.

00:21:57.600 --> 00:22:00.670
This is no time for joking! We're not turning back!

00:22:01.060 --> 00:22:03.920
That's the Princess I know, full of courage!

00:22:07.420 --> 00:22:10.680
Uh oh, this will be pretty close!

00:22:21.600 --> 00:22:24.360
Ensei! If we don't make it, you won't have your dinner tonight!

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:25.730
I'll do my best!

00:22:26.290 --> 00:22:28.950
Huh? It slowed down?

00:22:30.800 --> 00:22:32.200
Ready!

00:22:49.220 --> 00:22:51.250
Huh? Old man Hei?!

00:22:51.800 --> 00:22:54.090
Wh-Wha... Stop! You're kidding!

00:22:55.890 --> 00:22:58.390
Shoot! M-Mayor?!

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:03.610
Wait! Stop! Stop!

00:24:45.080 --> 00:24:47.390
Ensei, let's get into Korin Castle.

00:24:47.850 --> 00:24:51.210
Even if arrows rain down on us, we can evade them!

00:24:51.210 --> 00:24:52.030
Keep on going!

00:24:52.670 --> 00:24:55.050
Huh? Someone came out from Korin Castle?

00:24:55.550 --> 00:24:56.870
What? Mayor Hei?!
